    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Runbook: diagnosis, impact, recovery",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Triage and recovery\n\n**Overdue / stalled:** The age rule uses the first-available timestamp over PENDING, PUBLISHING, and RETRY_WAIT. Backoff and scheduler mode changes do not reset it, and unrelated successful publishes do not suppress it. Inspect status, `first_available_at`, `next_attempt_at`, attempts, leases, and `DEAD` transitions using the repository Operations guide. A `DEAD` event needs authorized review after checking Broker and consumer facts.\n\n**Scheduler:** Compare enabled, running, and last successful cycle age. Use `expected_scheduler=true` only when automatic scheduling is expected; set it false for intentionally disabled or manual-only runs. The rule includes a three-minute startup grace plus the 60-second demo poll window.\n\n**Snapshot:** Check `snapshot.failure`, database reachability, and application/database clock skew. Each target snapshot is filtered for freshness before replicas are grouped by logical `outbox_store`, so one fresh snapshot suffices and a stale large gauge cannot mask it. Automatic mode uses 60 seconds. Manual mode uses a fixed 120-second PromQL window; it must be edited explicitly if the planned manual refresh cadence changes. `periodic_enabled=0` does not suppress this monitor because automatic publication rounds may still refresh. Set `expected_snapshot=false` only where no refresh path is expected.\n\n**Status update failure:** A Broker receipt may exist while the Outbox remains unfinished, so duplicate delivery is possible. Check database write results and lease ownership; `PUBLISHED` does not prove consumer completion.\n\n**Missing first_available_at:** Do not infer age from `created_at`; review the M4.5 schema migration and inspect affected rows.\n\n**Send failure rate:** Check RocketMQ Proxy reachability, mappings, retry outcome and attempt limits. This warning requires at least five attempts in five minutes.\n\n**Recovery:** A timed alert enters firing only after its condition remains true for the configured `for` interval. Once the condition is false at a rule evaluation, the alert resolves at the next evaluation because these rules do not set `keep_firing_for`. New DEAD and failure-counter alerts also resolve when their increase window expires. Preserve the Prometheus/receiver evidence with the incident record.\n\nUse the Trace ID field at the top of this dashboard: paste a 32-character hexadecimal trace ID from an order request, then inspect the matching `POST /orders` → `reliable-event.register` → `reliable-event.publish` → `example.order.consume` spans and their parent IDs in the Trace panel below. Demo thresholds are not an SLA; tune against production backoff, poll, scrape, and business deadlines."
      }
    },
